{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Sorry we're late. The tram was a proper shambles and then there was nowhere to park out the front.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Have a seat. What can I do for you?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Um, nothing. Mum made me come.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's been crook since the other day and he just won't say it.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): From you, please. What's going on?",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (PATIENT): Bone pains. Couple of days. It's not that bad.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): Where?",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (PATIENT): Both thighs, and a bit in the lower back. Just a dull ache.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's been limping round the house. It's worse than a dull ache.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (PATIENT): I walked in here fine. It's a niggle, honestly.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sickle cell?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah. Known since I was a kid. Same old thing.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever?",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (PATIENT): A tiny bit warm. Nothing serious.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He was hot to touch last night. I nearly rang the clinic then.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Nurse. Obs, and what's on the med list.",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (NURSE): Temp's thirty seven point eight, pulse ninety six, blood pressure one eighteen over seventy two. Sats ninety eight percent. Breathing sixteen.",
  "[SEG0018] person_4 (NURSE): Chart says hydroxurea five hundred milligrams once a day, and folic acid five milligrams daily.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): Nah. The hydroxurea is a thousand milligrams, not five hundred. That chart's old.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): His haematologist put him up to one gram months back. I was at that appointment.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Every day?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah. Every day.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Not every day. I've found capsules still sitting in the blister pack.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (PATIENT): That's once in a blue moon. I take it.",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (NURSE): Sorry if I sound flat. My own boy's had an ear infection all week and I've barely slept. Your obs are done, though.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Cough?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Chest pain?",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He grabbed at his chest coming up the stairs this morning.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (PATIENT): I was stretching. There is no chest pain.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): Vomiting? Diarrhoea?",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (PATIENT): No. I was a bit queasy last night, that's all. Didn't actually vomit, and the bowels are fine.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): Stinging when you pee? Blood in the urine?",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (PATIENT): Nope.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): Headache? Blurred vision? Weakness down one side?",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (PATIENT): No. None of that.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (PATIENT): Never have.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): Alcohol?",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (PATIENT): A few beers on the weekend. Not through the week.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He lives at home with me. I'm his mum, if that helps.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any operations?",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (DOCTOR): Allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (PATIENT): No. Nothing.",
  "[SEG0046] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Penicillin. He came out in a rash all over when he was little, and we've avoided it ever since.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (PATIENT): I'm not even sure that happened. I had amoxil from the chemist last year and I was fine.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll have a feel. Tender over both thighs. No swelling, no redness. Chest is clear.",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (DOCTOR): This is a mild vaso-occlusive crisis. The sickle cells clog the little vessels in the bone, and that's what hurts. I'm not calling it a chest crisis.",
  "[SEG0050] person_3 (PATIENT): So it's nothing, then. I can just go.",
  "[SEG0051] person_2 (DOCTOR): Bloods first, today. Full blood count, reticulocytes, and kidney function. Push fluids, about three litres. Paracetamol one gram four times a day by mouth, and oxycodone five milligrams up to four times a day by mouth if the pain breaks through. I'll prescribe both.",
  "[SEG0052] person_3 (PATIENT): I don't need the oxycodone.",
  "[SEG0053] person_2 (DOCTOR): Have it there anyway. Don't go over that paracetamol dose. Reception will book you back in two days. If the fever climbs, you get short of breath, or the pain gets away from you, go to emergency, don't wait."
 ],
